//! Connected socket pair (`socketpair`) — the raw syscall boundary.
//!
//! One wrapper over POSIX `socketpair(2)`. No public `std` module uses it yet
//! (`std/net` builds its sockets through `std/sys/tcp` and `std/sys/unix`);
//! `tests/sys/socketpair.test.yo` is its only caller in this tree.
//!
//! ## Stability
//!
//! unstable — because the two platform behaviours are not the same object.
//! POSIX returns a real `AF_UNIX` pair; Windows has no `socketpair()` at all,
//! so the runtime emulates one with a loopback TCP `listen`/`connect`/`accept`
//! and hands back two TCP sockets. The error convention is `errno` on every
//! platform (the Windows runtime's socket-error sites translate WSA* codes,
//! 2026-10); what still differs is the OBJECT the promise is about. Freezing
//! needs a decision on whether this module promises
//! "two connected fds" (which the emulation satisfies) or "an `AF_UNIX`
//! pair with `AF_UNIX` semantics" (which it does not).
pragma(Pragma.AllowUnsafe);
{ __yo_sync_socketpair } :: import("./externs.yo");
/// Create a pair of connected sockets and write both descriptors into `sv`
/// (`sv[0]` and `sv[1]`, so the buffer must hold two `i32`s) — POSIX
/// `socketpair(2)`. Both ends are bidirectional; unlike `pipe`, either can
/// read and write. Returns 0 on success, a negative errno on failure.
///
/// Per platform:
/// * Linux and macOS — the real syscall, with `domain`, `sock_type` and
///   `protocol` passed straight through.
/// * Windows — emulated with a loopback TCP pair, so only `SOCK_STREAM` is
///   accepted (`-ENOTSUP` otherwise), `domain` must be one of
///   `AF_UNIX` / `AF_INET` / `AF_UNSPEC` (`-EAFNOSUPPORT` otherwise) and
///   `protocol` must be 0 or `IPPROTO_TCP` (`-EPROTONOSUPPORT` otherwise).
///   Failures are negated `errno` values, like the other platforms.
/// * wasm — `-ENOSYS`; Emscripten has no sockets.
socketpair :: (fn(domain : i32, sock_type : i32, protocol : i32, sv : *i32) -> i32)(
  __yo_sync_socketpair(domain, sock_type, protocol, sv)
);
export(socketpair);
